.TH SOUNDEX 1.SH NAMEsoundex \- the Soundex code of each word.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsoundex\fR< words.SH DESCRIPTION\fBsoundex\fRreads one name to a line on its standard input and prints its Soundexcode: the first letter and three digits for the consonants that follow,so names that sound alike share a code --\fBRobert\fRand\fBRupert\fRare both\fBR163\fR,\fR\fBSmith\fRand\fBSmyth\fRboth\fBS530\fR.\fRArguments are ignored; give it the names on its input.